{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on db3adddb. `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` keeps its value in the\ncutover window. Precondition 4 of plan 036 holds.\n\nWhy no object of the Grow Worker retries after the window:\n- A retired object returns from `alarm()` at once and sets no wake.\n- A new room pins the `base` family: Directory 27, Rules 15 and\n  Destination 21. The registry of `growArchivePolicies` holds the\n  two Grow definitions and the pins of the cohort\n  `ARCHIVE_DEVICE_APPLICATION_COHORT`: Register 17, Directory 16,\n  Membership 8, Rules 10 and Destination 12. So `admit` answers\n  false for each object of a new room, and the driver is disabled\n  for it.\n\nThe retry without end that you describe needs an object of the new\nformat whose definition the registry admits. The first place where\nthat can happen is the Grow install after CUT-R. So the first act\nof CUT-R gains item 6: whether a scope of the new release pins a\ndefinition that the registry admits, and what that scope does on\neach alarm until AE-1 lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}